    "content" : "In the time since my last post (about 90 minutes), I designed and printed this cable protector for the hole I drilled for the monitor cables. Since the hole had some jagged edges from the metal plating, I thought this was necessary. I designed it in Autodesk Inventor and it&#39;s extremely simple. Two concentric circles and extrudes of different lengths. I made it a little longer than the wall is thick so there is some extra support on the backside. Things like this are the perfect reason for 3D printers.",
    "objectType" : "note",
